          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can protein powder damage your kidneys?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In healthy people, research has not shown kidney damage from higher protein intakes, including the 1.6 to 2.2 g/kg range common among lifters. People with chronic kidney disease are a different case and are often advised to limit protein. If you have reduced kidney function or a history of kidney stones, check with your doctor or a registered dietitian first."
          }
